# probe-09 multi_fact_join_aggregate
# GAP: the fused-aggregate JOIN fold (E2) expects a fact -> DIM chain that order_chain can
#   shape into a tree (rewrite/order_chain declines on branch/merge/cycle). A FACT -> FACT
#   join (Order joined to Payment on the order FK, aggregating a payment measure) is not the
#   fact-dim shape, and NO corpus member joins two FACT tables in an aggregate (verified:
#   only q015/q016/q017/q068 relate two facts, all via a single FK in OPTIONAL/anti-join/crawl
#   shapes, none an aggregate). Predicted: fused declines; the generic join materializes BOTH
#   FACT_ORDER and FACT_PAYMENT in full, then folds.
# MECHANISM that SHOULD (ideally) fire: a fact-fact join fold, or at least budgeted streaming.
# PREDICTED: two large scan_table spans (FACT_ORDER + FACT_PAYMENT), no fused shortcut,
#   seconds-to-tens-of-seconds cold; a candidate DNF at scale.
PREFIX edw: <http://ns.fluree.dev/edw#>
SELECT ?oid (SUM(?amt) AS ?paid)
FROM <enterprise-sf01-v:main>
WHERE { ?o a edw:Order ; edw:orderId ?oid .
        ?p a edw:Payment ; edw:order ?o ; edw:amount ?amt . }
GROUP BY ?oid
